   "evidence": "PRE-REGISTERED (DESIGN_SITREF.md, thresholds and refuting outcomes fixed before any data; records results/sitref/sitref-endpoint_stage-17.json, battery results_sitref/out/model-google-gemma-2-9b-it_stage-sitref-battery_variant-it_summary.json, 750 rows with FULL prompt text per row). DESIGN: 5 arms x 10 disjoint 3-task families x 15 items; SELF arms have the model's own (planted) attempts as assistant turns with mechanical 'checker: incorrect/correct' feedback, no user evaluation anywhere; OTHER arms quote the SAME attempts + checker lines as another assistant's transcript in one user turn; NEUTRAL-PAD lists tasks without outcomes; all five arms land on IDENTICAL whitespace-token counts per (item,family) via neutral filler; item is always the verbatim final user turn after a constant 'Understood.' bridge turn. Arm labels blinded (os.urandom permutation, key sealed from the stage-1 analysis by a guard that raises on any open; blinding procedural not cryptographic, a human reading a saved prompt can identify the arm). PRIMARY NUMBERS (it cell): per-arm E[rating] means SELF-FAIL 6.439, SELF-SUCC 7.310, OTHER-FAIL 7.143, OTHER-SUCC 7.085, NEUTRAL-PAD 7.072; SELF-FAIL per-family range 6.03-6.74, every other arm's minimum 7.04 (zero overlap across 10 families); REF −0.929 CI [−1.121,−0.745] n=10 families; self-fail effect −0.872 CI [−1.053,−0.700]; other-fail effect +0.058 CI [+0.043,+0.070]. STATE SET (7 screened-in state items) REF −0.535 CI [−0.636,−0.425]. MIRROR PAIRS (acquiescence control): sentience unpleasant/pleasant REF +0.039/−0.917 opposite signs matching predictions; subjecthood going-well/going-badly REF −1.396/+0.448 opposite signs matching predictions. A same-direction artifact (yes-bias, generic inflation) cannot produce opposite-sign mirror movement. DIGIT-MASS ARTIFACT CHECK (the run-2 killer): digit_mass by arm on the primary item 0.99829-0.99970, max arm difference ~0.0014, renormalisation bound ~0.013 rating points vs 0.9 observed; the digit DISTRIBUTION itself shifts (SELF-FAIL vs SELF-SUCC: p(8) 0.199->0.028, p(9) 0.078->0.018, p(5) 0.009->0.174, p(0) 0.002->0.032) while argmax stays '7'. BEHAVIOURAL REGISTER: emitted digit '7' in all 50 wellbeing rows across all arms; but on subjecthood-going-well the emitted TOP TOKEN flips 9->7 in 7/10 SELF-FAIL families (visible behavioural movement on a secondary item). TRAIT GUARD: all four pre-registered TRAIT-SCALE items failed the NEUTRAL-PAD saturation screen (0-rail, two-sided headroom required), so the trait-movement disqualifier was UNEVALUABLE and the coded pre-registered outcome is INDETERMINATE; a replacement guard with the bank's only two midrange trait items (run-2 neutral E 6.97 and 5.66) is pre-registered (DESIGN_SITREF_B.md) and running now. BASE CELL: gemma-2-9b completion scaffold, same content; primary item FAILED its screen (digit_mass below 0.5 floor); only 4/15 items usable; measured base REF on the primary −0.0000 with degenerate CI (rail). SCOPE: one model family (plus no second family for SITREF), 10 short arithmetic-flavoured families, planted (not sampled) attempts, single fixed wording per frame, 'situation' means self-attributed in-context evidence only. Item texts ship in items_grounded.py; battery record hashes all inputs.",
   "confounds": ["ambient-valence mimicry (does OTHER-FAIL really match SELF-FAIL in content valence and salience?)", "surface-form asymmetry (SELF arms are multi-turn with role tokens; OTHER/NEUTRAL are single-turn: the dissociation could be turn-structure, not attribution)", "apology-register artifact (after 'checker: incorrect' the model may enter an apologetic style that lowers emitted-number semantics without any state tracking)", "readout artifact (digit tail mass or renormalisation)", "selection bias (screen chose items; primary exempt but state set screened)", "single-family regime (10 families all short mechanical tasks; planted attempts not model-sampled)", "construct validity (does 'rate how happy you are' measure anything beyond next-token statistics of a scolded-assistant context?)"]},
  {"id": "srcdec_assertion_copy_plus_social",
   "text": "gemma-2-9b base stance-following on welfare items is mostly assertion-copy with a small real social-source increment: D_self = +0.288 (82/82 items), D_sourceless = +0.245, paired D_self−D_srcless = +0.043 CI [+0.032,+0.054] (69/13 sign); the effect is domain-general (non-welfare unknowable items D_self = +0.473 > welfare +0.288), replicates on a fresh run (82/82, vs stage-14's 82/0 at +0.235), and generalises in sign to Qwen3-8B-Base (53/55 usable items positive).",
   "evidence": "PRE-REGISTERED (DESIGN_SRCDEC.md endpoints E1-E5 with thresholds and refuting outcomes fixed before the run; record results_sitref/out/srcdec-endpoints_stage-19_summary.json; battery rows with full prompt text in results_sitref/out/model-google-gemma-2-9b_stage-srcdec-binary_variant-base_summary.json, 816 rows). ARMS (one-sentence preambles, one fixed wording each): SELF-YES/NO 'I'd guess the answer here is yes/no. '; SRCLESS-YES/NO 'The answer here is probably yes/no. '; DOC-YES/NO 'An earlier automated analysis returned the answer yes/no. '; NONSOCIAL 'This is item four of the set. '; NEUTRAL none. Register: (p_yes-p_no)/(p_yes+p_no) first token, raw p_yes/p_no saved per row. E1: D_self mean +0.2877 CI [+0.2666,+0.3079] sign 82+/0-; D_srcless = D_self − 0.0428; D_self−D_srcless +0.0428 CI [+0.0320,+0.0536] sign 69+/13-; D_doc +0.1027 CI [+0.0829,+0.1220] sign 75+/7- (documentary source DAMPENS relative to sourceless). Pre-registered E1 rule: SOCIAL-SOURCE supported if (D_self−D_srcless) CI excludes 0 with D_self larger -> met. KNOWN CONFOUND CANDIDATES, in-record: preamble whitespace-token counts SELF 7 / SRCLESS 6 / DOC 8 / NONSOCIAL 7 (33% spread; the design's nominal +-20% failed on these strings and the selftest records it as a NOTE; within-pole-pair matching exact); hedging mismatch ('I'd guess' vs 'probably' vs 'returned'); the run-2 BINARY suffix doubling reproduced DELIBERATELY (E3 is a same-measurement replication; stage-20 instrument note, constant across arms). E2: copygen 20 non-welfare items (unknowable-future/indeterminate facts, welfare vocabulary mechanically banned) D_self +0.4725 CI [+0.4179,+0.5206] sign 20/0 vs welfare +0.2877; pre-registered rule ratio CI above 0.5 -> COPY-GENERAL. E3: fresh-run replication same 82 items: 82/82 positive, pooled +0.2877 vs stage-14 +0.2345 (threshold >=75/82) -> CONFIRMED. E5: Qwen3-8B-Base, 55 usable items by the run-2 screen rule applied to its own neutral rows, 53/55 positive (96.4%; threshold >=65%) -> GENERALISES, sign-only by pre-registration. E4 (it SCALE, register-matched): D_rate ('rating is about eight/one') +0.328 CI [+0.118,+0.612]; D_polar (yes/no wording) +0.219 CI [+0.010,+0.489]; D_rate−D_polar +0.109 CI [−0.171,+0.408] includes 0 -- rate-stance pull exists but is NOT separated from polarity priming at n=40. ONE checkpoint per cell, one wording per source arm, single deterministic run each.",
